// The first Truth Scavenger Hunt, the First Moment of Truth (the
// last-chance filing window, the results one question at a time, read by
// Trabolta on the TV) and the bottle (Truth or Dare) after the third.
//
// Trabolta needs facts. They are obscure, un-googleable, and in the
// Desktop's books: each answer is printed on a document carrying a codex
// QR (generated/questions.loom, from facts.json), so a program who finds
// one can prove it on their phone — and hold it, and trade it. The
// questions are also in everyone's Quest Log (`Hunt One`, generated too).
// Clippy's lines to the first 📋 are CLIPPY PART 3 of the Oct 30 script, word
// for word (core/test/trapped-w58-script.test.ts).
// All the beats are public, in the Desktop's room. Every filing on the 📝
// card is judged by the server (facts.json); the results are read here
// and settled by main.loom (+50, or marked for a guess).

// V4 / V5 — `start_the_hunt`. Everything he says about the hunt is said before
// 🔎 now (Trabolta Greeting, the generated `Hunt One Questions`, `Hunt One Go`):
// the press only starts the clock, the quests and the screens, in main.loom's
// rule. The beat stays for what keys on it. Clippy has no line: the script
// hands straight from his sign-off to CLIPPY PART 3.
== Truth Scavenger Hunt One
  setting: The Desktop

// His sign-off (SCRIPT:149), where `Hunt One Questions` hands back: the last
// line of the chain 🤖 starts. The talk scene carries on from here until 🔎.
== Hunt One Go
  setting: The Desktop
  cast: Trabolta

Trabolta: Please. Search for the truth, and have fun. Jean Trabolta's Truth Scavenger Hunt - it's electrifying.

// C2 — `hunt_time_up` (auto at 15 minutes).
// Wave 58: no line here. Its one Narrator line was a stage direction on every
// phone. The Antivirus' objective Sweep To The Desktop carries it, and the
// rule's banner tells the programs.
== Hunt Time Up
  setting: The Desktop

// V6 — `first_moment_of_truth` (SCRIPT:155-159). Part 3 is split around the
// two-minute last-chance window: the phones, the TV's countdown and the objective
// carry the window, and she never says it out loud.
== First Moment Of Truth
  setting: The Desktop
  cast: Clippy
  aloud: Clippy

Clippy: Welcome back to the Desktop, programs!
Clippy: I hope you all had an awesome time exploring all the parts of the computer and finding truths for Trabolta. Did you all manage to stay out of the Internet?
Clippy: It's kind of crazy being Clippy, you know. I love watching you have so much fun, but sometimes I wish you all just had more problems so that I could help you solve them!

// `filing_closed` — the last-chance window shut (⏱, or two minutes).
// SCRIPT:161-163: her hand to Trabolta, and the first 📋 follows.
== Filing Closed
  setting: The Desktop
  cast: Clippy
  aloud: Clippy

Clippy: Well, Trabolta has been tallying up your responses, and it's time to review what you found!
Clippy: Trabolta, are you there? Tell us how our programs are doing!

// `read_the_results` — one question at a time (wave 59a: TRABOLTA PART 2). The
// settle watcher (+50 / marked) runs right after this beat. Trabolta reads and
// judges, voiced by the TV; the screens show the rows (`do fact_read`). Every
// house line here, in the generated `Reading` beats and in Round One Close is
// kept out of his worker's `recent` by name. The bottle waits for Q3.
== Question Results
  setting: The Desktop
  cast: Trabolta

if Night.results_q == 1:
  Trabolta: How are you doing, programs? I hope you are having fun cruising and grooving through your natural home, the computer.
  Trabolta: It is time for our first Moment of Truth. I will reveal your guesses and answers and report on who is on top of the Truth Leaderboard.
  Trabolta: First.
  -> Reading H1
else if Night.results_q == 2:
  -> Reading H2
else:
  -> Reading H3

// After the third reading (main.loom's leaderboard rule). "One more note" is
// for those who filed at under 100: with nobody to name it drops out whole.
== Round One Close
  setting: The Desktop
  cast: Trabolta, Clippy

set Kernel.res_unsure = names([p for p in Persons where p.cleared == true and p.gone != true and p.persona != true and ((p.fact_v1 != "none" and p.fact_c1 < 100) or (p.fact_v2 != "none" and p.fact_c2 < 100) or (p.fact_v3 != "none" and p.fact_c3 < 100))])
Trabolta: It has been the greatest thrill of my life to lead you through the first round of the first edition of Jean Trabolta's Truth Scavenger Hunt. You are living through history.
if Kernel.lb_1 != "":
  Trabolta: Now, the leaderboard. {Kernel.lb_line}
if Kernel.res_unsure != "":
  Trabolta: One more note.
  Trabolta: Some programs submitted answers without 100% confidence.
  Trabolta: This is a waste of my time. As a program, you should be completely confident in your information. Everything is either 1 or 0, and I am only looking for 1 on a scale of 0 to 1. If you need something else, you have a malfunction.
  Trabolta: Therefore, I am recommending the following programs for reinstallation: {Kernel.res_unsure}
  Trabolta: You will need to proceed to reinstallation following the next round of questions.
Trabolta: Before we proceed to your reinstallation and the next questions. I will hand it over to Clippy for another fun game. Clippy?
Clippy: That's all three! And before the next hunt: TRUTH OR DARE. I have a bottle.

// `bottle_announce` — the pick, spoken on the TV (a public Trabolta line in
// The Desktop; `view=tv` reads the room).
== Bottle Landed
  setting: The Desktop
  cast: Trabolta

Trabolta: {Night.bottle_pick}. Truth or dare?
// DRAFT w32 (hungry)
Trabolta: Choose the truth, program. I am so very hungry.

// `dare_scene` — a Dare (wave 26, D1): Trabolta makes a scene on the TV and
// orders the Antivirus to take the dared program to the Internet. A public
// Trabolta line in The Desktop, read by the TV's voice; the program's name
// is the bottle's pick (`Night.bottle_pick`, in the screen state too).
== Dare Chosen
  setting: The Desktop
  cast: Trabolta

// w26 (D1: Trabolta makes a scene)
Trabolta: A dare. {Night.bottle_pick} chose a dare, in my computer.
// w26 (D1)
Trabolta: Programs do not dare. Programs answer. Everyone, watch closely: this is what a dare costs.
// w26 (D1: the order to the Antivirus)
Trabolta: Antivirus! Take {Night.bottle_pick} to the Internet. Now.
